    "body": "## Purpose\nIntroduce a small, controlled Fusion-side automation runner and local Python CLI so VanDesign can validate actual CAD geometry without repeated manual Fusion UI interactions.\n\n## Changes\n- Fusion Python add-in with controlled job execution and read-only/design-allowlisted operations.\n- Local JSON job schema, queue, CLI, execution journaling, policy checks and evidence packaging.\n- Example inspect/measure/batch jobs; runner installation instructions.\n- Automation unit tests and CI integration.\n\n## Reported verification (Claude Desktop; independent review pending)\n- A real-Fusion automated demonstration reportedly passed all 7/7 steps, with baseline restored and no residual edits.\n- Negative tests reportedly rejected an incorrect expectation and a duplicate job ID.\n- Local automation suite reportedly passed 44/44; foundation suite passed 5/5; G3 prototype tests also passed.\n- Claude-reported benchmark: approximately 0.13 s per automated edit-plus-measure cycle versus 59–69 s with manual Computer Use. These timings need independent scope/method review before treating the ratio as definitive.\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n- **Draft only. Do not merge.**\n- Base: `feature/v5-g3-cabinet-variants`, because the runner depends on its G3 interfaces; the base is still unmerged.\n- The PR must not be retargeted to `main` or `develop` until the G3 integration strategy is agreed.\n- Existing G2 designs and protected Fusion installations must remain unchanged.\n- This is a development/testing tool, not manufacturing qualification.\n\n## Reviewer acceptance\nConfirm source and evidence provenance, validation expectations, duplicate-ID and failure handling, safe Fusion API execution context, baseline restoration, CI status, and real-world timing methodology.\n\nNext product focus after this runner: G4 safe incremental regeneration, then the first visible van-interior demonstration.",
